<p>In the latest development, President Trump used a 19-minute prime-time address from the White House on April 1 to argue that the U.S. campaign against Iran is close to achieving its goals, while also warning that U.S. forces will hit Iran “extremely hard” for another two to three weeks. Across outlets, the clearest new tension was between his message that the campaign is nearing completion and his failure to offer a firm path to end the fighting, even as he suggested the war could wrap up within weeks. Trump again framed the war as necessary to prevent Iran from obtaining a nuclear weapon and said battlefield gains had sharply reduced Iran’s military capacity. But Iranian officials rejected his separate claim that Tehran had asked for a ceasefire, calling it false and baseless, while the broader conflict continued to rattle energy markets and keep pressure on the Strait of Hormuz, a vital shipping route for global oil supplies. For readers worldwide, the immediate takeaway is that Washington is signaling possible escalation rather than a clearly defined diplomatic exit, leaving both regional security and global energy prices highly sensitive to what happens in the next few weeks.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7CYuJCaSbUb-X7n-HYFQLcUt9jrG7EmypqyfQYKpCRXbmEuAmViHYO6PZL1UrLrQH8n0qqxFTUAZB4asvOejdoyOJ7yzwawsCA_rZRgGxjXVI6QOS3WdvQh7RAk0CnDo0GTAlTrVdQnbgZc0Yz0hsBoBjblEqiwa9M7Mx0vVLD_HTTJgF1fTw6dZWYMyXa-8b713yhOm0yANIz9WrbFj0Ct_XnVaO3pRtFIt07NFf7689M5ccraE4_H43irhLbQFGJoCjSkBfU25RS4mKw' alt='President Donald Trump speaks about the Iran war from the Cross Hall of the White House on Wednesday in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Hormuz pressure: Trump urged countries that depend on oil flowing through the Strait of Hormuz to take the lead in protecting the waterway, saying the United States imports almost no oil through it.</li><li>Comparative framing: Trump tried to present the campaign as short and manageable by contrasting it with longer U.S. wars and insisting any gasoline-price pain would be temporary.</li><li>No big reveal: Although the White House billed the speech as an operational update, Trump did not announce a ceasefire, troop drawdown, or any other concrete policy shift.</li><li>Mixed messaging: Coverage highlighted inconsistencies in Trump&#x27;s messaging, including whether a negotiated deal is necessary and whether reopening the Strait of Hormuz is a firm condition for ending operations.</li></ul><blockquote>We are going to hit them extremely hard over the next two to three weeks. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: Officials argued the war had already crippled much of Iran&#x27;s military machinery, with Trump citing destroyed weapons factories and severe losses to naval and air capabilities as proof the operation was working. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/trumps-white-house-address-on-the-middle-east-war-irans-navy-gone-air-force-in-ruins-leaders-are-dead-11299610#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>, <a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/president-donald-trump-warns-iran-of-power-grid-strikes-if-no-deal-is-reached-read-full-text-of-trump-speech-on-iran-war-middle-east-conflict-11299810#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Iranian government: Tehran&#x27;s response went beyond denying Trump&#x27;s ceasefire account; Iranian officials also signaled that any halt in fighting would require guarantees that hostilities would not simply resume. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-iran-president-requests-ceasfire-tehran-says-false/article70812864.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Domestic political observers: Several reports framed the address as an effort to reassure a war-weary public and stop approval slippage as Americans focused on gasoline prices and the conflict&#x27;s duration. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-to-address-nation-as-iran-war-batters-approval'>The Straits Times</a>, <a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-speech-iran-war/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>European observers: European coverage noted that Trump barely mentioned NATO while still pressing allies and oil-importing states to take on more responsibility for security around the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/podcast/berlin-playbook-podcast/rede-zur-nation-wie-trump-im-iran-weiter-machen-will/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/01/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news'>Trump Claims Military Success but Offers No Clear Timeline to End Fighting</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/hopes-dim-for-swift-end-to-iran-war-after-trump-speech-oil-prices-surge-anew'>Hopes dim for swift end to Iran war after Trump speech, oil prices surge anew</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/trump-iran-war-address-ceasefire-hormuz/33722964.html'>Trump Says US Near &#x27;Finishing the Job&#x27; in Iran, But Vows &#x27;Two To Three Weeks&#x27; Of More War</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/3af1d6e5-2a61-47f9-af65-efeb1b859ab9'>Trump threatens to hit Iran ‘extremely hard’ in coming weeks</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-us-objectives-in-iran-nearing-completion/article70814015.ece'>Trump says U.S. objectives in Iran ‘nearing completion’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-says-us-campaign-nearing-completion/live-76635831'>Iran war: Trump says US campaign &#x27;nearing completion&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636981-iran-war-us-israel-trump/'>Trump vows to hit Iran ‘extremely hard’ as Tehran denies talks (VIDEOS, PHOTOS)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/trump-threatens-to-escalate-iran-war-but-says-end-is-very-close-11300258#publisher=newsstand'>Trump Th